      "text": "To solve for \\( f(2) \\), let's start by understanding the given functional equation:\n\n\\[ f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 4^x \\]\n\nWe can iterate this equation by substituting \\( \\frac{1}{x} \\) for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - 2 f(x) = 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\]\n\nThen we can combine the two equations:\n\n\\[ f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 4^x \\]\n\\[ 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - 2 f(x) = 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\]\n\nAdding these two equations:\n\n\\[ f(x) - 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) + 2 f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - 2 f(x) = 4^x + 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\]\n\\[ -2 f(x) = 4^x + 4^{\\frac{1}{x}} \\]\n\\[ f(x) = -\\frac{4^x + 4^{\\frac{1}{x}}}{2} \\]\n\nNow we need to find \\( f(2) \\):\n\n\\[ f(2) = -\\frac{4^2 + 4^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{2} \\]\n\\[ f(2) = -\\frac{16 + 4^{1/2}}{2} \\]\n\\[ f(2) = -\\frac{16 + 2}{2} \\]\n\\[ f(2) = -\\frac{18}{2} \\]\n\\[ f(2) = -9 \\]\n\nHence, the final answer is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{-9} \\]\n```python\n# Define the function based on the derived formula\ndef f(x):\n    return - (4**x + 4**(1/x)) / 2\n\n# Calculate f(2)\nresult = f(2)\nprint(result)\n```",
